  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conserving the threatened jaguar population through improved management of human jaguar conflicts within the Southern Belize Biological Corridor</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project will reduce conflicts between humans and jaguars throughout the Southern Belize Biological Corridor through the adoption of jaguar conflict mitigation measures by cattle farmers. This project is intended to conserve the Near Threatened jaguar (Panthera onca) population by addressing impacts of direct persecution and retaliatory killings by humans. Specific activities include: (1) development and implementation of a system to monitor human-jaguar conflicts locally and to support national monitoring efforts; (2) recruitment of interested livestock farmers buffering the corridor to implement jaguar conflict mitigation measures within their farms; (3) development and implementation of a public campaign focused on human-jaguar conflict mitigation targeting communities buffering the corridor to encourage the protection of jaguars and increase the number of reports of human jaguar conflicts to relevant authorities.</narrative>
  </description>
